  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-06-05T19:29:58.258Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "# Suggestion\nAllow us to export VRChat worlds as standalone Unity application.\n# How it's good for world creators\nWe would be able to reach a wider audience, not being restricted to VRChat. Thus incentiving us to make more awesome worlds.\n# How it's good for VRChat Inc.\nVRChat thrives because of its user generated content. By empowering world creators, everyone benefits.\nVRChat could also as for a % cut from game sales made with VRChat's SDK.\n# Suggested implementation\nMake ClientSim & the VRChat SDK able to export standalone Windows builds, offline single-player only.\n# Specific examples\n- Dr. Morro makes some beautiful VRChat worlds. Being able to share them outside VRChat would certainly allow him to get more recognition for his work.\n- The Devouring was so good that they're remaking it as a standalone game, outside VRChat. Imagine if its creators had been able to export it, sell it, and give VRChat a share of the profits.\n- Creators might be attracted to VRChat as a platform, upon discovering they could reach more users that way.\n# Concerns\n- Creators might be led off VRChat as a platform, upon discovering they could reach more users that way.",
